    },
    {
     "id": "C",
     "text": "$-\\sqrt{10}$"
    },
    {
     "id": "D",
     "text": "$-3.15$"
    },
    {
     "id": "E",
     "text": "$-\\frac{22}{7}$"
    }
   ]
  },
  "answer": {
   "choices": [
    "E"
   ]
  },
  "explanation": "All are negative, so the greatest is the one nearest 0, i.e. the one with the smallest absolute value. As decimals: $\\frac{19}{6}\\approx3.167$, $3.17$, $\\sqrt{10}\\approx3.162$ ($3.16^2 = 9.9856$, $3.17^2 = 10.0489$), $3.15$, $\\frac{22}{7}\\approx3.143$. The smallest is $\\frac{22}{7}$, so $-\\frac{22}{7}$ is greatest.",
  "choiceExplanations": {
   "A": "$-3.167$ is farther from 0 than $-3.143$.",
   "B": "$-3.17$ is the farthest from 0 of the five.",
   "C": "$-3.162$ is farther from 0 than $-3.143$.",
   "D": "$-3.15$ is farther from 0 than $-3.143$."
  },
